hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16810","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Haytham ibn Kharija narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwa from Yusuf ibn Sulayman from his grandmother Maymuna from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sanna that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Islam began as something strange, then it will return as something strange as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and who are the strangers? He said: Those who set things right when the people become corrupt. And by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, faith will surely retreat to Medina as the flood retreats, and by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, Islam will surely retreat to what is between the two mosques as the snake retreats to its hole."
